# The rclone-manager-tests commit this repository's gate runs its browser
# e2e suite and its CLI smoke slice from. Moved by
# scripts/e2e/bump-tests-pin.sh, and the commit that moves it is itself
# gated against the new pin, so a bad bump cannot land unnoticed.
#
# Why this repository pins that one, and that one pins a build of this one:
# pinning the tests repository means a new or changed test cannot break
# unrelated in-flight work here until someone bumps this line, and the bump
# is itself gated. Pinning the product build over there means a release
# cannot silently change what those suites certify. Each is one line, in one
# file, reviewable on its own.
#
# At a794c38, read off rclone-manager-tests' merged main rather than a branch
# head, because a squash rewrites the head and the pin then names a commit in
# no history. It is exactly two commits past the sha this line held before, and
# both are #431's, so nothing unrelated arrives with the bump.
#
# Those are rclone-manager-tests#32 and rclone-manager-tests#33, which between
# them retire the two retention cases that recorded this binary's old note
# about FR-20 being unimplemented and replace them with one that asserts the
# note that replaces it. They are the specs half of #431; the product half is
# in the same branch as this bump, because either one alone leaves the gate
# red. The second of the two exists because I committed the first without
# staging two of its files, and that repository's own lockstep test caught it
# on main.
#
# This header used to narrate a deliberate hold at 9dfd6e3, waiting for #240's
# Suite B specs to have a product to run against. #240 landed, b2092a5 moved
# the sha to 57ef7b5, and nobody came back to the paragraph explaining the
# hold, so it went on describing a hold that had already ended. Worth a
# sentence rather than a silent delete: a comment nobody returns to is the same
# defect #431 is about, one file over.
#
# The hold was the arrangement working as designed, and the design has not
# changed. Specs are allowed to land over there ahead of the feature they
# describe, and this line is what stops them being enforced here until the
# feature arrives. Move the pin past a spec whose product change is not in this
# tree and that spec goes red; the gate catches it, which is the pin doing its
# job rather than a problem with it.
#
# It runs the other way too, and that half has no automation. rclone-manager-
# tests carries its own build-under-test.json naming a commit of THIS
# repository, and a spec landed ahead of its feature cannot go green over there
# until somebody moves it. Both of those commits are in that position right
# now: they need that file moved to #465's own merge commit.
TESTS_REPO_URL=https://github.com/spdrman/rclone-manager-tests.git
TESTS_REPO_SHA=a794c38581d3c2f7df73e3bee9753c063fc9d72a
